  "body": "What changed:\r\n- `OpParams::Bore` has an `entry` field (plunge, ramp, helix). Plunge is the default and is\r\n  not written to the project file.\r\n- The links' approach `ramp_angle` and `helix_angle` cap every descent.\r\n- A bore with entry ramp or helix may use up to 4096 ring-ramp legs (`MAX_BORE_ZIG_LEGS`). The\r\n  plunge bore keeps the 64-leg limit, so a non-centre-cutting tool is still refused by name.\r\n- The Bore pane has an Entry group. Arc is refused by name in the generator.\r\n\r\nReadings (Ø3.175 tool, 5 degree cap, 1 mm stepdown, 3 mm deep):\r\n- Ø3.2 hole: worst descent 5.00 degrees (main: 6 axial dives).\r\n- Ø3.5 hole: 5.00 degrees. Ø6 hole: 5.00 degrees (Ramp), 4.55 degrees (Helix; main: 13.4).\r\n- Axial moves left: the named re-plunge down the column the ring just cut, one a level.\r\n- A Ø3.2 hole posts about 5,400 moves for 3 levels. A 5 mm stepdown at 5 degrees on that\r\n  ring needs more than 4096 legs and keeps the named axial dive.\r\n\r\nPinning tests:\r\n- `camcraft-motion`: `bore_ramp_angle` (`a_bore_barely_wider_than_its_cutter_descends_within_the_angle_cap`, `a_plunge_bore_ignores_the_ramp_and_helix_angles`)\r\n- `camcraft-app`: `bore_entry` (`a_bore_entry_ramp_or_helix_caps_the_descent_on_a_hole_barely_wider_than_the_tool`, `a_bore_refuses_the_arc_entry_by_name`, `a_bore_entry_round_trips_and_the_default_is_not_written`)\r\n\r\nNot exercised:\r\n- The 4 to 14 mm STEP plate from the report (the model is not in the repository).\r\n- The Mach4 post output.\r\n- The GUI Entry group (no new UI test).\r\n- The heavy lanes.\r\n- MCP: `edit_operation` writes the same params, so `entry` rides it. No new command. No new MCP tool.\r\n\r\nQuick gate (`CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=4 cargo xtask gate quick`, Windows, `core.autocrlf=true`, 1183 steps): all other steps ok. Red: those named below. On the final rerun `egui_app`, `trace_composite` and `clippy` were green and `trace_parity` crashed.\r\nBaseline: the same steps on unmodified `origin/main` (run by name):\r\n- `sinumerik_810m_post`, `catalog_render` and `egui_app` are red on main too. The first two read a\r\n  golden or example file that the CRLF checkout changed. `egui_app` exits 101 on main.\r\n- `trace_composite` and `trace_parity` crash with an access violation on both main and the\r\n  branch, on some runs and not on others (main: 3 of 3 manual runs crashed, 2 gate runs passed).\r\n- `clippy -D warnings` is green on main and on this branch.\r\nNo red step is new on this branch.\r\n\r\nChangelog: Bore operations can enter by ramp or helix. The approach angles cap the descent, down to a hole 0.025 mm wider than the tool.\r\n\r\nFixes #3828\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n",
